  "id": "childhood-apraxia-of-speech",
  "term": "childhood apraxia of speech",
  "definition": "Childhood apraxia of speech is a severe neurodevelopmental speech disorder in which a child has difficulty planning and coordinating the movements needed to produce speech sounds. It is marked by features such as a limited range of consonants, vowel mistakes, and inconsistent production of words, and is thought to reflect motor discoordination.",
